NAME
       nslookup - look up names and addresses in DNS

SYNOPSIS
       nslookup NAME [SERVER]

DESCRIPTION
       nslookup asks a DNS server for the address of NAME (or the name of an
       address) and prints the server it used and the answer. Without SERVER
       it uses the first nameserver in /etc/resolv.conf. It comes with the
       bind-utils package, together with host and dig, which are often more
       convenient.

       nslookup asks DNS only. It does not read /etc/hosts; getent hosts NAME
       shows what programs on the machine really get.

EXAMPLES
           nslookup server2.lab.example.com
           nslookup 192.168.50.12
           getent hosts server2

SEE ALSO
       host(1), dig(1), getent(1), resolv.conf(5)
